    <string name="tutorial_page1_title">Welcome to RemEx</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page1_body">RemEx is your remote PC management command center. Control your computer, launch apps, monitor performance, and even view your desktop — all from your phone.\n\nLet\'s get you connected in a few quick steps.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_page2_title">Install the Host First</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page2_body">Before you can connect, you need the RemEx host software running on your PC.\n\nOption 1 — RemEx Desktop Client\nDownload and run Remex.Client.Desktop on your PC. It bundles the host automatically — just launch it and the host starts in the background.\n\nOption 2 — RemEx Host (standalone)\nInstall and run Remex.Host as a standalone service. This is ideal for headless servers or if you only need the host.\n\nBoth are self-contained — no extra runtimes needed. Download the latest publish folder from the GitHub releases page, extract, and run.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page2_link_label">Download from GitHub Releases</string>

    <string name="tutorial_page3_title">Auto-Discovery</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page3_body">The easiest way to connect is automatic discovery.\n\n1. Make sure Remex.Client.Desktop or Remex.Host is running on your PC\n2. Ensure both your phone and PC are on the same Wi-Fi network\n3. Tap \'Discover Automatically\' on the Connection screen\n\nRemEx uses mDNS to detect running hosts on your local network. Your PC\'s IP and port will be filled in automatically.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_page4_title">Finding Your IP Address</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page4_body">If auto-discovery doesn\'t work, you can connect manually. First, find your PC\'s local IP address:\n\nWindows:\n  Open Command Prompt → type ipconfig\n  Look for \'IPv4 Address\' (e.g. 192.168.1.42)\n\nmacOS:\n  System Settings → Network, or run:\n  ipconfig getifaddr en0\n\nLinux:\n  Run ip addr or hostname -I\n\nYou can also see the IP address in the Remex.Client.Desktop window under the connection status section.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_page5_title">Manual Connection</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page5_body">Once you have your IP address:\n\n1. Go to the Connection screen (Settings → Connection)\n2. Enter your PC\'s IP address\n3. Enter the port (default is 5005)\n4. Tap \'Save &amp; Connect\'\n\nRemEx will establish a connection and you\'ll see your PC\'s status appear on the dashboard.\n\nRemember: Remex.Client.Desktop or Remex.Host must be running on the target PC for the connection to succeed.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_page6_title">You\'re All Set!</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page6_body">You\'re ready to take control.\n\nFrom the dashboard you can monitor system stats, launch apps, manage tasks, and stream your desktop remotely.\n\nHead to Personalization to customize your theme, card shapes, fonts, and colors.\n\nCheck out the FAQ in Settings if you run into any issues. Enjoy RemEx!</string>

    <!-- New tutorial page: QR Code Pairing (inserted as page 3) -->
    <string name="tutorial_page_qr_title">Quick Pair with QR Code</string>
    <string name="tutorial_page_qr_body">The fastest way to connect is by scanning a QR code.\n\n1. Open Remex.Client.Desktop on your PC\n2. Go to Connection → Show QR Code\n3. On your phone, tap the QR icon on the Connection screen\n4. Point your camera at the code\n\nYour phone will automatically save and connect — no manual typing needed!</string>

